diff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md
index 9e4648c3c..c1cc4bc5e 100644
--- a/docs/design.md
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -493,6 +493,7 @@ How the generated SPIR-V expects the runtime to work:
 | Out-of-bounds typed buffer loads and `DST_SEL=1` | When a MUBUF `buffer_load_format_{x,xy,xyz,xyzw}` or `buffer_load_format_d16_{x,xy,xyz,xyzw}` is out of bounds (`OOB_SELECT` 0–3, `num_records == 0`, partial-element spill, or swizzled OOB), memory is not accessed and raw data channels (`DST_SEL` 4..7) read 0, while the V# `DST_SEL` swizzle still runs: `DST_SEL=0` returns 0 and `DST_SEL=1` returns `1.0f` (`0x3F800000`, `d16` `0x3C00`) iff V# `FORMAT[6:0]` is a valid float, normalized or scaled buffer format (`1..77` ending in `_UNORM`, `_SNORM`, `_USCALED`, `_SSCALED`, or `_FLOAT`), and integer `1` (`0x00000001`, `d16` `0x0001`) for `UINT`/`SINT`, `INVALID` (`0`), and reserved codes (`78..127`). `d16_x` and `d16_xyz` preserve the unaddressed upper 16 bits of the final destination VGPR, and MTBUF `tbuffer_load_format_*` ignores V# `DST_SEL` on both out-of-bounds and `FORMAT=0` loads (returning 0 in addressed channels). Until 2026-11-22 `Gen.buffer_load_format` clamped the post-swizzle result to 0 when `in_b` was false (`SHADER-429`), dropping `DST_SEL=1` on out-of-bounds loads and returning `1.0f` instead of `1` for `DST_SEL=1` with `FORMAT=0`. **Hardware-verified on RDNA2** (`gfx1036`, Windows 11, driver `32.0.21042.62`, wave32 and wave64, 746 kernels via `tools/hw_oracle`: all 41 `Gen.FORMATS` across `xyzw`/`d16_xyzw`/`d16_xyz`/`d16_x`, all 128 7-bit `FORMAT` codes `0..127` for both `f32` and `d16`, `OOB_SELECT` 0–3, partial spill, swizzled OOB, MTBUF controls, and inactive EXEC lanes), Vulkan GPU-checked across all 128 7-bit `FORMAT` codes (`xyzw`, `d16_xyzw`, `d16_xyz`, `d16_x`) and the `cs_fmt_*`/`cs_oob_*`/`cs_bounds`/`cs_buf_*` fixtures on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (driver `32.0.16.1088`) and AMD Radeon Graphics (`gfx1036`, driver `32.0.21042.62`), and CPU/`spirv-val`-checked by `tests/semantic/test_buffer_oob_dst_sel.py`. |
 | `v_div_fixup_f32` | Measured natively on an AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics RDNA2 GPU (`gfx1036`, not the console's `gfx1013`; Windows driver 32.0.21042.62, `tools/hw_oracle`, wave32 and wave64 identical on every case: 256 seeded triples across 4 MODEs plus 73 targeted special-case/modifier rows, 0 mismatches). Computes `div_fixup_f32(S0=quotient, S1=denom, S2=numer)` with pure integer SPIR-V ops under the game's inferred MODE (`IEEE=0`, `denorm32=0`, `DX10_CLAMP=1`): VOP3 `abs` (clear bit 31) then `neg` (flip bit 31) apply bitwise to `S0`/`S1`/`S2` before classification (including NaN payloads); `S1`/`S2` subnormals flush to signed zero (`exp == 0`) while `S0` subnormals are preserved; priority order is (1) `NaN(S2) → S2`, (2) `NaN(S1) → S1` (signalling NaNs pass unchanged under `IEEE=0`, quieted only when `IEEE=1`), (3) `0/0` or `±inf/±inf → 0xFFC00000` (`-qNaN`), (4) `zero(S2) ∨ inf(S1) → ±0.0`, (5) `zero(S1) ∨ inf(S2) → ±inf`, (6) `exp(S2) − exp(S1) ≤ −151 → ±0.0` (pure biased-exponent check, beats `NaN(S0)` and `inf(S0)`; no overflow check), (7) `NaN(S0) → ±inf`, (8) `copysign(S0, sign(S1) ⊕ sign(S2))`. Output modifiers `mul:2`/`mul:4`/`div:2` apply before `clamp`, and `clamp` maps NaN to `+0.0` (`DX10_CLAMP=1`) before `FClamp` to `[0, 1]`. Not modelled: `IEEE=1` sNaN quieting, `denorm32=3` keeping `S1`/`S2` subnormals, and the hardware `omod` `-0 → +0` quirk (same as the other f32 ops). Checked bit-for-bit against 73 measured `gfx1036` words in `tests/semantic/test_alu_div_fixup_f32.py`. |
 | Atomic natural alignment, 64-bit bounds, and `buffer_atomic_{fmin,fmax}` | Measured natively on RDNA2 (AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics, `gfx1036`, Windows driver `32.0.21042.62`, wave32 and wave64 via `tools/hw_oracle/`): **natural alignment** is enforced on every 32-bit and 64-bit buffer/global atomic (`buffer_atomic*`, `buffer_atomic*_x2`, `global_atomic*`, `global_atomic*_x2`), even under `OOB_SELECT = 2` (DISABLED). A 32-bit atomic requires `(addr & 3) == 0` (`offset = 1, 2` and `base + 2, offset = 0` are dropped; `base + 2, offset = 2` succeeds) and a 64-bit `_x2` atomic requires `(addr & 7) == 0` (`offset = 2, 4` and `base + 4, offset = 0` are dropped; `base + 4, offset = 4` succeeds). When dropped (OOB or unaligned), memory is untouched, an active `glc` lane receives `0` (32-bit) or `(0, 0)` (64-bit) in `vdst`/`vdata`, and an inactive lane (`EXEC = 0`) preserves `vdst`/`vdata`. Independently confirmed on a second `gfx1036` (driver `24.10.24`): without the alignment guard, an unaligned SPIR-V `OpAtomicAdd` corrupts the aligned dword (`100 -> 0xDEADBEF3`), whereas with the guard memory stays untouched and `0` is returned. `Gen.atomic_aligned` guards all six atomic emitters on `addr & 3 == 0` / `addr & 7 == 0`, merges `0` via `OpPhi` on skipped paths, and writes through `Gen.dst` so inactive lanes keep their prior register value while active unaligned/OOB lanes receive `0`. **64-bit partial bounds (`buffer_atomic*_x2`)**: the same `gfx1036` wave32/wave64 measurements confirm the all-or-nothing 8-byte bounds rule (`fixed_fmt = 62`) across all four `OOB_SELECT` modes (answering the unmeasured note in the `buffer_atomic_{and,or,xor,swap}_x2` row): mode 3 (RAW) requires `offs + 8 <= num_records` (`0/8` and `8/16` succeed; `0/7`, `0/5`, `0/4`, `8/15`, `8/12` drop cleanly); mode 0 (STRUCTURED_WITH_OFFSET) requires `idx < num_records` and `off + 8 <= stride` (`stride = 8, off = 0`, `stride = 16, off = 8`, `stride = 12, off = 0` succeed; `stride = 7, off = 0` and `stride = 12, off = 8` drop); mode 1 (STRUCTURED) checks `idx < num_records`; mode 2 (DISABLED) checks `num_records != 0`. **`buffer_atomic_{fmin,fmax}`**: lowered via `Gen.buffer_atomic_float` sharing `Gen._emit_atomic_fminmax_cas` (relaxed Device-scope `OpAtomicLoad` seed + `OpAtomicCompareExchange` + `GLSL.std.450` `NMin`/`NMax` CAS loop, no float-atomic extension required), enforcing V# bounds, 4-byte alignment, and `glc` return (`lds` and non-1-VGPR `vdata` raise `Unsupported`). On `gfx1036`, normal floats, `±inf`, `-0` vs `+0` (`fmin(-0, +0) = -0`, `fmax(-0, +0) = +0`), and `qNaN` (returns the non-NaN operand) match `NMin`/`NMax`; **known approximation**: the `gfx1036` L2 atomic unit quiets `sNaN` (`0x7f800001 -> 0x7fc00001`) regardless of `MODE`, while f32 subnormal handling follows the wave's `MODE.denorm32` and preserves sign (independently verified on a second `gfx1036`, wave32/wave64: under `denorm32 = 0`, subnormals flush to signed zero — `fmax(0x80000001, 0x80000002) -> 0x80000000 (-0)`, `fmax(0x00000001, 0x00000002) -> +0` — whereas under `denorm32 = 3`, subnormals are preserved and `NMin`/`NMax` is exact); `NMin`/`NMax` does not model `sNaN` quieting or `denorm32 = 0` subnormal flushing. CPU-checked by `tests/semantic/test_buffer_atomic_fminmax_and_align.py` (value grid, multi-lane CAS contention, OOB/partial-bounds matrix, inactive vs active-unaligned distinction across all six atomic families, and SPIR-V structural checks). |
+| Compare `SDST` (`null`, `exec`/`exec_lo`) and wave32 `vcc_hi` lane masks | `Gen.compare` (`f64` and `write_compare_result`), `Gen.cmp_class`, `Gen.cmp_class_f64`, and the 64-bit integer compare paths route `SDST` through `Gen.mask_dst` (`Gen.is_mask_dst` validates `v_cmp_class_f64`), so `v_cmp_*_e64` and `v_cmp_class_f64_e64` accept `null` (discarding the mask write without altering `VCC` or `EXEC`), `exec_lo` (wave32) / `exec` (wave64) (narrowing `EXEC` via `SDST[lane] = EXEC[lane] ? cond : 0` with inactive lanes remaining off even on constant `tru`/`t` predicates, leaving `VCC` untouched), and `vcc_hi` in wave32, while still raising `Unsupported` on VGPR/literal destinations and on `vcc_hi` VALU destinations in wave64. In wave32 (`not wave64`), `vcc_hi` (`0x6b`) is an independent 32-bit scalar/mask register (`%vcc_hi`), separate from `vcc_lo`/`VCC` (`%vcc`): `tools/lane_masks.py` (`kind`/`put`/`step`) tracks `"vcc_hi"` separately from `"vcc"` when `wave64=False`, and `Gen.mask_dst`, `Gen.holds_lane_mask`, `Gen.mask_src`, `Gen.mask_half` (`None` in wave32), `Gen.wave_mask`, and `Gen.wqm` store/load `%vcc_hi` as a per-lane mask when `"vcc_hi"` is tracked and extract bit `lane & 31` when `%vcc_hi` holds plain scalar data. Source: RDNA2 ISA VOPC/VOP3 `SDST` encoding (`0x7d` `null`, `0x7e` `exec_lo`/`exec`, `0x6b` wave32 `vcc_hi`), confirmed with `llvm-mc -arch=amdgcn -mcpu=gfx1013` (wave32 and `-mattr=+wavefrontsize64`). CPU-checked by `tests/test_lane_masks.py` (`test_wave32_vcc_hi_isolation`) and `tests/semantic/test_vcmp_dst_wave32_vcchi.py` (`spirv_mini_interp`, `spirv_wave_interp`, `spirv-val --target-env vulkan1.2` across wave32, wave64 native, and `--wave64-emulate`); translated SPIR-V compute shaders executed on AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics (`gfx1036`, wave32 + wave64 native + `--wave64-emulate`) and AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (`vk_compute_test`). **No raw RDNA2 hardware-oracle run and no corpus count.** |
 
 ### System values confirmed on the corpus (SHADER-4)
 
diff --git a/tests/semantic/test_vcmp_dst_wave32_vcchi.py b/tests/semantic/test_vcmp_dst_wave32_vcchi.py
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..239b7a4b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/semantic/test_vcmp_dst_wave32_vcchi.py
@@ -0,0 +1,490 @@
+"""Semantic tests for v_cmp_* / v_cmp_class_f64 null/exec/wave32-vcc_hi SDSTs and wave32 vcc_hi masks.
+
+Covers:
+  - null destination on v_cmp_* (f32, f16, u16, i16, u32, i32, f64, f/tru_f64, u64 eq/lt, i64) and v_cmp_class_f64:
+    mask write is discarded without touching VCC or EXEC (wave32, wave64, and --wave64-emulate)
+  - exec_lo (wave32) and exec (wave64 / --wave64-emulate) destinations on the same compare / class families:
+    active lanes update EXEC and inactive lanes remain off (including constant tru/t compares), while VCC stays intact
+  - wave32 vcc_hi as an independent 32-bit mask/scalar register:
+      * v_cmp_*, v_cmp_class_f64, v_add_co_u32, v_mad_u64_u32, s_and_saveexec_b32, s_wqm_b32 writing vcc_hi
+      * v_cndmask_b32_e64, v_add_co_ci_u32_e64, s_bcnt1_i32_b32, s_ff1_i32_b32, s_flbit_i32_b32,
+        v_mbcnt_lo_u32_b32, s_cmp_eq/lt_u32, s_wqm_b32 reading vcc_hi (preserving vcc_lo)
+      * plain scalar data in vcc_hi (e.g. 0xA5000005, s_wqm_b32 vcc_hi, 1) read both as scalar and as a lane-bit
+        mask without corrupting or reading vcc_lo
+  - negative controls rejecting invalid destinations (VGPR everywhere; vcc_hi SDST in wave64)
+  - Vulkan 1.2 SPIR-V validation via spirv-as / spirv-val when present on PATH
+"""
+import gc
+import os
+import shutil
+import struct
+import subprocess
+import sys
+import tempfile
+import unittest
+import warnings
+
+HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
+ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE))
+TOOLS_DIR = os.environ.get("LEONIDA_TOOLS_DIR") or os.path.join(ROOT, "tools")
+
+sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
+if HERE not in sys.path:
+    sys.path.insert(0, HERE)
+if TOOLS_DIR not in sys.path:
+    sys.path.insert(0, TOOLS_DIR)
+
+import rdna2spirv  # noqa: E402
+import spirv_mini_interp as si  # noqa: E402
+import spirv_wave_interp as wi  # noqa: E402
+
+STUB_DXBC = b"DXBC" + bytes(24) + struct.pack("<I", 0) + bytes(4)
+VSHARP = [0, 0, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0x31016FAC]
+
+
+def _fssm_blob(wave_size):
+    blob = bytearray(0x138)
+    blob[0:4] = b"FSSM"
+    if wave_size == 32:
+        struct.pack_into("<I", blob, 0xD4, 0x20)
+    return bytes(blob) + struct.pack("<4I", 0x8088, wave_size, 1, 1)
+
+
+def _validate_spirv(name, spv):
+    spirv_as = shutil.which("spirv-as")
+    spirv_val = shutil.which("spirv-val")
+    if not spirv_as or not spirv_val:
+        return
+    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:
+        asm_p = os.path.join(d, "s.spvasm")
+        bin_p = os.path.join(d, "s.spv")
+        with open(asm_p, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
+            f.write(spv)
+        r1 = subprocess.run([spirv_as, "--target-env", "vulkan1.2", asm_p, "-o", bin_p],
+                            capture_output=True, text=True)
+        assert r1.returncode == 0, f"spirv-as failed for {name}: {r1.stderr}"
+        r2 = subprocess.run([spirv_val, "--target-env", "vulkan1.2", bin_p],
+                            capture_output=True, text=True)
+        assert r2.returncode == 0, f"spirv-val failed for {name}: {r2.stderr}"
+
+
+def _translate_cs(name, body_lines, wave_size=32, emulate=False):
+    prev_emu = rdna2spirv.WAVE64_EMULATE
+    try:
+        rdna2spirv.WAVE64_EMULATE = emulate
+        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:
+            os.mkdir(os.path.join(tmp, "disasm"))
+            os.mkdir(os.path.join(tmp, "fssm"))
+            s_path = os.path.join(tmp, "disasm", "cs_" + name + ".s")
+            with open(s_path, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
+                f.write(f"; cs_{name}\n")
+                for ln in body_lines:
+                    f.write(f"\t{ln}\n")
+                f.write("\ts_endpgm\n")
+            with open(os.path.join(tmp, "cs_" + name + ".dxbc"), "wb") as f:
+                f.write(STUB_DXBC)
+            with open(os.path.join(tmp, "fssm", "cs_" + name + ".fssm"), "wb") as f:
+                f.write(_fssm_blob(wave_size))
+            with warnings.catch_warnings():
+                warnings.simplefilter("ignore", ResourceWarning)
+                spv = rdna2spirv.translate(s_path)
+                gc.collect()
+            assert rdna2spirv.translate.last_gen.wave64 == (wave_size == 64)
+            return spv
+    finally:
+        rdna2spirv.WAVE64_EMULATE = prev_emu
+
+
+def _run_cs(name, body_lines, wave_size=32, emulate=False, validate=True):
+    spv = _translate_cs(name, body_lines, wave_size=wave_size, emulate=emulate)
+    if validate:
+        _validate_spirv(name, spv)
+    pc = VSHARP + [0] * 28
+    mem = {}
+    sg_size = 32 if emulate else wave_size
+    si.run_workgroup(
+        spv, wave_size, sg_size,
+        inputs_for=lambda i: {"%wg_id": (0, 0, 0), "%local_id": (i, 0, 0), "%sg_lane": i % sg_size},
+        push_constants=pc, memory=mem,
+    )
+    return mem
+
+
+def _run_vs_w32(name, body_lines, out_regs=("v10", "v11", "v12", "v15")):
+    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:
+        os.mkdir(os.path.join(tmp, "disasm"))
+        os.mkdir(os.path.join(tmp, "fssm"))
+        s_path = os.path.join(tmp, "disasm", "vs_" + name + ".s")
+        with open(s_path, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
+            f.write(f"; vs_{name}\n")
+            for ln in body_lines:
+                f.write(f"\t{ln}\n")
+            f.write("\tv_mov_b32_e32 v20, 0\n")
+            f.write("\texp pos0 v20, v20, v20, v20 done\n")
+            f.write(f"\texp param0 {', '.join(out_regs)}\n")
+            f.write("\ts_endpgm\n")
+        with open(os.path.join(tmp, "vs_" + name + ".dxbc"), "wb") as f:
+            f.write(STUB_DXBC)
+        with open(os.path.join(tmp, "fssm", "vs_" + name + ".fssm"), "wb") as f:
+            f.write(_fssm_blob(32))
+        with warnings.catch_warnings():
+            warnings.simplefilter("ignore", ResourceWarning)
+            spv = rdna2spirv.translate(s_path)
+            gc.collect()
+        assert rdna2spirv.translate.last_gen.wave64 is False
+    _validate_spirv("vs_" + name, spv)
+    res = wi.run_wave(spv, wave=32, builtins={"VertexIndex": lambda lane: lane, "InstanceIndex": lambda _lane: 0})
+    return [lane_out["%out_param0"] for lane_out in res["outputs"]]
+
+
+COMPARE_NULL_EXEC_CASES = [
+    # (tag, setup_lines, insn_template_with_dst, cond_fn)
+    ("f32", [
+        "v_cvt_f32_u32_e32 v1, v0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v2, 10.0",
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_f32_e64 {dst}, v1, 10.0", lambda i: i < 10),
+    ("f16", [
+        "v_cvt_f32_u32_e32 v1, v0",
+        "v_cvt_f16_f32_e32 v1, v1",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v2, 0x4500",      # 5.0 in f16
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_f16_e64 {dst}, v1, v2", lambda i: i < 5),
+    ("u16", [
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v1, v0",
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_u16_e64 {dst}, v1, 9", lambda i: i < 9),
+    ("i16", [
+        "v_sub_nc_u32_e32 v1, v0, 6",
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_i16_e64 {dst}, v1, 0", lambda i: (i - 6) < 0),
+    ("u32", [], "v_cmp_lt_u32_e64 {dst}, v0, 11", lambda i: i < 11),
+    ("i32", [
+        "v_sub_nc_u32_e32 v1, v0, 7",
+    ], "v_cmp_gt_i32_e64 {dst}, v1, 0", lambda i: (i - 7) > 0),
+    ("f64", [
+        "v_cvt_f64_u32_e32 v[2:3], v0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v4, 0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v5, 0x40180000",  # 6.0
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_f64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], v[4:5]", lambda i: i < 6),
+    ("f_f64", [
+        "v_cvt_f64_u32_e32 v[2:3], v0",
+    ], "v_cmp_f_f64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], v[2:3]", lambda i: False),
+    ("tru_f64", [
+        "v_cvt_f64_u32_e32 v[2:3], v0",
+    ], "v_cmp_tru_f64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], v[2:3]", lambda i: True),
+    ("u64_eq", [
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v2, v0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v3, 0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v4, 4",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v5, 0",
+    ], "v_cmp_eq_u64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], v[4:5]", lambda i: i == 4),
+    ("u64_lt", [
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v2, v0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v3, 0",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v4, 8",
+        "v_mov_b32_e32 v5, 0",
+    ], "v_cmp_lt_u64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], v[4:5]", lambda i: i < 8),
+    ("class_f64", [
+        "v_cvt_f64_u32_e32 v[2:3], v0",  # lane 0 is +0.0 (bit 6 = 0x40); lanes >= 1 are +normal (bit 8 = 0x100)
+    ], "v_cmp_class_f64_e64 {dst}, v[2:3], 0x100", lambda i: i >= 1),
+]
+
+
+class VcmpDstWave32VccHiTests(unittest.TestCase):
+    def _native_modes(self):
+        return [(32, False), (64, False)]
+
+    def test_null_destination_preserves_vcc_and_exec(self):
+        for wave_size, emulate in self._native_modes():
+            vcc_reg = "vcc_lo" if wave_size == 32 else "vcc"
+            mov_exec = "s_mov_b32 exec_lo, -1" if wave_size == 32 else "s_mov_b64 exec, -1"
+            and_exec = "s_and_b32 exec_lo, exec_lo, vcc_lo" if wave_size == 32 else "s_and_b64 exec, exec, vcc"
+            for idx, (tag, setup, tmpl, _cond_fn) in enumerate(COMPARE_NULL_EXEC_CASES):
+                with self.subTest(wave=wave_size, emulate=emulate, case=tag):
+                    # Initial active mask: even lanes (i & 1 == 0) via v_and_b32 + v_cmp_eq_u32.
+                    lines = [
+                        "v_and_b32_e32 v10, 1, v0",
+                        "v_mov_b32_e32 v11, 0x77777777",
+                        "v_mov_b32_e32 v12, 0x88888888",
+                        f"v_cmp_eq_u32_e64 {vcc_reg}, v10, 0",
+                        *setup,
+                        and_exec,
+                        # VCC sentinel: lanes with (v0 & 3) == 2 (distinguished from active mask!)
+                        "v_and_b32_e32 v13, 3, v0",
+                        f"{mov_exec}",
+                        f"v_cmp_eq_u32_e64 {vcc_reg}, v13, 2",
+                        # Re-apply even-lane EXEC before v_cmp null, so both active and inactive lanes run null compare.
+                        "v_cmp_eq_u32_e64 s4, v10, 0" if wave_size == 32 else "v_cmp_eq_u32_e64 s[4:5], v10, 0",
+                        "s_mov_b32 exec_lo, s4" if wave_size == 32 else "s_mov_b64 exec, s[4:5]",
+                        tmpl.format(dst="null"),
+                        # Record which lanes stayed active in v11, and restore full EXEC to read VCC in v12.
+                        "v_mov_b32_e32 v11, 0x11111111",
+                        mov_exec,
+                        f"v_cndmask_b32_e64 v12, 0x22222222, 0x33333333, {vcc_reg}",
+                        "v_lshlrev_b32_e32 v14, 3, v0",
+                        "v_add_nc_u32_e32 v15, 4, v14",
